# counter_unroute.def snippet — qflow/qrouter workaround for net _9_
#
# If `qflow route` reports:
#   Error:  Tap position N,N layer 1 not marked as source!
#   List of failed nets follows: _9_
# then net _9_ (driver _33_/NAND2X1.Y -> _34_/NAND2X1.B) needs a fixed
# pre-route segment.  The 2um-wide cell-LEF pins line up exactly on the
# routing pitch, so some taps land on grid boundaries and never get marked
# as source.  Add the segment below to counter_unroute.def inside NETS,
# copy counter_unroute.def over counter.def, and re-run qrouter.sh.
#
# Coordinates below assume the usual placement:
#   _33_ NAND2X1 + PLACED ( 1700 3100 ) N    -> Y pin abs (24,44)-(26,46)
#   _34_ NAND2X1 + PLACED ( 2650 3100 ) FN   -> B pin abs (30,50.5)-(32,52.5)
# Re-derive them from your counter.def if the placement differs.

- _9_
  ( _34_ B )
  ( _33_ Y )
+ ROUTED metal2 ( 2500 4600 ) ( * 4700 ) M2_M3
  NEW metal3 ( 2500 4700 ) ( 3100 * ) M3_M2
  NEW metal2 ( 3100 4700 ) ( * 5100 ) ;
